Independently enumerated local-function edges reachable from both policy-compliance entries. The historical admission graph reaches only policy/census selectors, exact artifact/config authentication, pure envelope/reserve calculations and data-only package/prefix/report composition. It does not reach live role admission, the live frontier loader, enrollment/freshness/recovery, wall/monotonic clocks, nonce generation, provider/API calls or operational construction. Local imports of existing data types do not construct operational services.

Independent AST inspection found all four admission-module typed-state calls and all 23 historical-verification typed-state calls explicitly pass `repair=False`. The preserved completed-history launch read likewise uses `repair=False`; projection passes it through `_authorities` to policy-source reads. Focused ledger inspection confirms `load_role_ledger_records` authenticates legacy shapes and raises `RoleLedgerMigrationRequiredV5`; its parameter named migration authority does not execute migration. The remaining approved immutable history/resource paths are unchanged, supported by their exact source hashes and prior reviews; they were not broadly re-audited.

Independently compiled both frozen modified byte strings in memory without importing source or producing bytecode. Independently verified old-class AST preservation, the exact original historical body, changed-definition scope and newline evidence described above. The complete `implementation-report.md` was read before verdict; it records scoped Ruff PASS, in-memory compile PASS and static/protection inspection without warnings. Ruff is implementer evidence, not rerun here.

